### A doc comment whose body has shape.

The formatter used to trim every line of a block comment, which flattened
anything indented inside one: an example, a list, a table. A comment is not
in the tree, so neither the reparse check nor the fuzzer can see inside one.
Only a case like this can.

    let indented: "four spaces"
        let deeper: "eight"

  - a list item
    continued underneath it

The blank line above and the one below are part of it too.

###
say "after the block"

# An ordinary comment is still just trimmed.
say "end"
